(6489422, 964444, 23484, '<td valign="top">Excellent HDR.</td>', 'Excellent HDR.', '2011-08-02 20:05:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489428, 961943, 59796, '<td valign="top">Belated Happy Birthday to the subject - hope it was a good one.<br/>The candles are perfectly exposed in the picture, with nice colors too! Everything else is too dark though. Happy Birthday is a happy occasion, and the picture needs to be bright and cheerful to depict it. If necessary, I''d expose one for the candles, and one for everything else, and then combine the exposures into a HDR.</td>', 'Belated Happy Birthday to the subject - hope it was a good one.The candles are perfectly exposed in the picture, with nice colors too! Everything else is too dark though. Happy Birthday is a happy occasion, and the picture needs to be bright and cheerful to depict it. If necessary, I''d expose one for the candles, and one for everything else, and then combine the exposures into a HDR.', '2011-08-02 20:19:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489430, 964416, 59796, '<td valign="top">Nice capture! The baby and mommy scene is always heart warming :)<br/>The picture might do better with a boost in saturation - right now, the green reflections look washed out. I''d also crop it differently to move the red eye as much away from the center as possible, because that''s where my attention is drawn to in the first instance.</td>', 'Nice capture! The baby and mommy scene is always heart warming :)The picture might do better with a boost in saturation - right now, the green reflections look washed out. I''d also crop it differently to move the red eye as much away from the center as possible, because that''s where my attention is drawn to in the first instance.', '2011-08-02 20:22:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489432, 964690, 59796, '<td valign="top">Nice expressions! And neat processing too. I wish the grandpa (2nd from the right) would also look where everyone else seems to be looking - would''ve made a better scene I think.</td>', 'Nice expressions! And neat processing too. I wish the grandpa (2nd from the right) would also look where everyone else seems to be looking - would''ve made a better scene I think.', '2011-08-02 20:24:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489440, 962856, 59796, '<td valign="top">Bad hair day for sure :)<br/>Nice and sharp! Love the creamy and subtle pastel bokeh to go with it.<br/>Can''t help but notice the sensor dust on the center-right edge as well as on 2/3 right-top edge.</td>', 'Bad hair day for sure :)Nice and sharp! Love the creamy and subtle pastel bokeh to go with it.Can''t help but notice the sensor dust on the center-right edge as well as on 2/3 right-top edge.', '2011-08-02 20:39:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489453, 963502, 47470, '<td valign="top">This shows great technical control of lighting, especially the fine rim light on his face and shoulder.  His expression is beautiful because it does truly look genuine.  To be a bit picky, there is a bit of harsh clipping in the blacks showing on my monitor, and the sharpening is a little over-done for my taste.  I would have also preferred if less of his face was cropped on the left side; I can''t seem to verbalize quite why I feel that way besides saying that it feels like an uncomfortable place to crop someone''s face--though maybe the uncomfortableness works with the image''s emotion.  It''s nice to crop close when the model has such a telling expression, but because of the particular emotion showed, I wonder if it would have worked better with more negative space for another tangible/physical representation of hurt, pain, worry, anxiety, and/or isolation.<br/> <br/>While I''d consider this image to be on the right side of the bell curve for portraits, for me to bump it up any higher, I would need to see something more than just a beautiful, technically sounds visual representation of the subject at a specific point in time.  I want to see some kind of story, some kind of deeper insight into the subject.  Basically, I think this is a great image, but I know what kind of talent lurks beneath the surface of the photographers on DPC, and I want to push that talent to its limit : )</td>', 'This shows great technical control of lighting, especially the fine rim light on his face and shoulder.  His expression is beautiful because it does truly look genuine.  To be a bit picky, there is a bit of harsh clipping in the blacks showing on my monitor, and the sharpening is a little over-done for my taste.  I would have also preferred if less of his face was cropped on the left side; I can''t seem to verbalize quite why I feel that way besides saying that it feels like an uncomfortable place to crop someone''s face--though maybe the uncomfortableness works with the image''s emotion.  It''s nice to crop close when the model has such a telling expression, but because of the particular emotion showed, I wonder if it would have worked better with more negative space for another tangible/physical representation of hurt, pain, worry, anxiety, and/or isolation. While I''d consider this image to be on the right side of the bell curve for portraits, for me to bump it up any higher, I would need to see something more than just a beautiful, technically sounds visual representation of the subject at a specific point in time.  I want to see some kind of story, some kind of deeper insight into the subject.  Basically, I think this is a great image, but I know what kind of talent lurks beneath the surface of the photographers on DPC, and I want to push that talent to its limit : )', '2011-08-02 20:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489463, 964309, 47470, '<td valign="top">It took me a minute to understand exactly what was going on in this image, but before I figured it out, the title gave a great atmosphere for the abstract nature of the image.  Cool capture.</td>', 'It took me a minute to understand exactly what was going on in this image, but before I figured it out, the title gave a great atmosphere for the abstract nature of the image.  Cool capture.', '2011-08-02 20:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489470, 964265, 59796, '<td valign="top">A very difficult high-contrast scene exposed nicely (although the white chest looks a bit blown).<br/>My focus is immediately drawn to the eye of the bird, which ended up close to the center of the pic. I would crop the pic differently to keep the eye as close to the thirds as possible, and away from the center. Although the reflection wouldn''t be clear, a full reflection would look better than a chopped off one I think.</td>', 'A very difficult high-contrast scene exposed nicely (although the white chest looks a bit blown).My focus is immediately drawn to the eye of the bird, which ended up close to the center of the pic. I would crop the pic differently to keep the eye as close to the thirds as possible, and away from the center. Although the reflection wouldn''t be clear, a full reflection would look better than a chopped off one I think.', '2011-08-02 20:57:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489474, 964857, 47470, '<td valign="top">I wish you had processed the image to match the time period.</td>', 'I wish you had processed the image to match the time period.', '2011-08-02 21:01:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489477, 964849, 47470, '<td valign="top">I would have preferred to see this cropped closer.  I do love the monochrome and the soft tones.</td>', 'I would have preferred to see this cropped closer.  I do love the monochrome and the soft tones.', '2011-08-02 21:03:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489480, 964347, 113156, '<td valign="top">Wonderful, looks like a hospital bed.</td>', 'Wonderful, looks like a hospital bed.', '2011-08-02 21:04:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489481, 963793, 47470, '<td valign="top">The tones in the falling water are really beautiful and are pushed right to the edge of being clipped in the white without actually being clipped (which is how I think it should be).  I don''t really like the foreground though.  It does give a bit on context, but it disrupts the smoothness of the rest of the image.  I don''t think the image would have worked without the foreground, but I wonder if different processing on that part of the image would have worked better.</td>', 'The tones in the falling water are really beautiful and are pushed right to the edge of being clipped in the white without actually being clipped (which is how I think it should be).  I don''t really like the foreground though.  It does give a bit on context, but it disrupts the smoothness of the rest of the image.  I don''t think the image would have worked without the foreground, but I wonder if different processing on that part of the image would have worked better.', '2011-08-02 21:06:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489482, 964558, 113156, '<td valign="top">A great face she has, nice candid and lovely rich tones.</td>', 'A great face she has, nice candid and lovely rich tones.', '2011-08-02 21:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489483, 963807, 47470, '<td valign="top">I wish the lighting on his face would have taken into account the purple-magenta light in front of him, possibly in the form of a tint to his skin or as a brighter spot where that light would really be hitting him, leaving the other side of his face and his hands more in shadow.</td>', 'I wish the lighting on his face would have taken into account the purple-magenta light in front of him, possibly in the form of a tint to his skin or as a brighter spot where that light would really be hitting him, leaving the other side of his face and his hands more in shadow.', '2011-08-02 21:09:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489484, 964853, 59796, '<td valign="top">Nice! Soft lighting and gentle colors show off the waterfalls very well. An apt title adds to the charm.<br/>I wonder how the scene would look from the other side of the falls - right now it feels as though the slope of the hill top leads the eye away from the waterfalls.</td>', 'Nice! Soft lighting and gentle colors show off the waterfalls very well. An apt title adds to the charm.I wonder how the scene would look from the other side of the falls - right now it feels as though the slope of the hill top leads the eye away from the waterfalls.', '2011-08-02 21:10:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6489488, 964075, 59796, '<td valign="top">Battle for survival? <br/>Amazing scene captured precisely, and in such nice light, and with a creamy/dreamy bokeh! Very well done indeed.</td>', 'Battle for survival? Amazing scene captured precisely, and in such nice light, and with a creamy/dreamy bokeh! Very well done indeed.', '2011-08-02 21:12:42.000000', NULL, 1),
