(6498790, 963502, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vikas:</b></div><hr/><i> Great portrait, those eyes are razor sharp and show a lot of emotion. IMO it would have looked amazing in B&amp;W, also being advanced editing I would have removed the white spots in the background and t-shirt to clean up the shot - another suggestion is the crop from left needs to be a just a tad bit more. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks for the thoughts Vikas, I did sample it in b&amp;w but the lightly desated color version got good feedback over at 500px so I went with that. The white spots were intentional however. I have taken to using baby powder in different ways in shots lately. Like <a href="//500px.com/photo/1172270" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here.</a></td>', 'Originally posted by vikas: Great portrait, those eyes are razor sharp and show a lot of emotion. IMO it would have looked amazing in B&W, also being advanced editing I would have removed the white spots in the background and t-shirt to clean up the shot - another suggestion is the crop from left needs to be a just a tad bit more.   thanks for the thoughts Vikas, I did sample it in b&w but the lightly desated color version got good feedback over at 500px so I went with that. The white spots were intentional however. I have taken to using baby powder in different ways in shots lately. Like here.', '2011-08-09 01:37:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6498801, 964361, 66398, '<td valign="top">This was my favorite shot in the challenge and now everytime I log into dpc I get to see it and it keeps getting more and more beautiful to me. It is such a lovely shot and it stands out even in a thumbnail.</td>', 'This was my favorite shot in the challenge and now everytime I log into dpc I get to see it and it keeps getting more and more beautiful to me. It is such a lovely shot and it stands out even in a thumbnail.', '2011-08-09 02:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
