(6499446, 960399, 134120, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, they are all very helpful.  This picture was my first time using a Macro lens attachment and I was focused on the flower when the bee just kinda flew into the picture.  I only had a second to react so I was pretty happy with it considering I wasn''t planning on catching it.  It would have been nice if the wings were in focus as well.  I think the center of the flower would have been since that was what i was focused on before the bee arrived breifly :(<br/> <br/>All in all, I was happy to share and get feedback.  Considering the wind was blowing and the lens wasn''t quite focused and it was my first time using it, I will take it.  I don''t think I even made any digital adjustments, it was presetned as shot.<br/> <br/>Thansk again, I will keep trying!<br/> <br/>Jennifer</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, they are all very helpful.  This picture was my first time using a Macro lens attachment and I was focused on the flower when the bee just kinda flew into the picture.  I only had a second to react so I was pretty happy with it considering I wasn''t planning on catching it.  It would have been nice if the wings were in focus as well.  I think the center of the flower would have been since that was what i was focused on before the bee arrived breifly :( All in all, I was happy to share and get feedback.  Considering the wind was blowing and the lens wasn''t quite focused and it was my first time using it, I will take it.  I don''t think I even made any digital adjustments, it was presetned as shot. Thansk again, I will keep trying! Jennifer', '2011-08-09 16:53:46.000000', NULL, 0),
